      ],
      "source": "https://encyclopediaofalabama.org/article/columbia/"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Between 1822 and 1833, Columbia served as the trading hub for the Wiregrass Region and was the county seat of Henry County.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Columbia%2C_Alabama"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Old Columbia Jail, built during the Civil War, stands as one of Alabama's oldest surviving jails.",
